{"step_index":106,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T18:58:14Z","thinking":"**Developing Animation Logic**\n\nOkay, I'm currently working on `src/scenes/radius.tsx` to define the animation. I'm leveraging `write_to_file` to create this essential part. The code structure for this file will be imported, in order to get the functionality working.\n\n\n**Defining Animation Steps**\n\nI've been examining the 2D elements. I've successfully incorporated a basic structure with Circle and Txt components. Refactoring the scene setup is now underway, and I'm adding `heatText` to display an animation. I am progressing with defining the animation flow: initially revealing the pipe, then growing insulation to a critical radius.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import {makeScene2D, Circle, Txt} from '@motion-canvas/2d';\\nimport {createRef, waitFor, easeInOutCubic} from '@motion-canvas/core';\\n\\nexport default makeScene2D(function* (view) {\\n  const pipe = createRef<Circle>();\\n  const insulation = createRef<Circle>();\\n  const text = createRef<Txt>();\\n  const heatText = createRef<Txt>();\\n\\n  view.add(\\n    <>\\n      <Circle\\n        ref={insulation}\\n        width={200}\\n        height={200}\\n        fill=\\\"#e74c3c\\\"\\n        opacity={0.5}\\n      />\\n      <Circle\\n        ref={pipe}\\n        width={200}\\n        height={200}\\n        fill=\\\"#34495e\\\"\\n      />\\n      <Txt\\n        ref={text}\\n        y={-300}\\n        fill=\\\"#ffffff\\\"\\n        fontSize={48}\\n        text=\\\"Critical Radius of Insulation (r_c = k / h)\\\"\\n      />\\n      <Txt\\n        ref={heatText}\\n        y={300}\\n        fill=\\\"#ffffff\\\"\\n        fontSize={40}\\n        text=\\\"Bare Pipe (No Insulation)\\\"\\n        textAlign=\\\"center\\\"\\n      />\\n    </>\\n  );\\n\\n  // 1. Initial State\\n  yield* waitFor(1);\\n\\n  // 2. Growing insulation UP to Critical Radius\\n  yield* heatText().text(\\\"Adding Insulation (Below Critical Radius)\\\\nHeat Loss INCREASES!\\\", 1);\\n  yield* insulation().size(400, 2, easeInOutCubic);\\n  \\n  yield* waitFor(1);\\n  yield* heatText().text(\\\"Critical Radius Reached (r = r_c)\\\\nHeat Loss is at MAXIMUM\\\", 1);\\n  yield* insulation().fill(\\\"#f1c40f\\\", 0.5); // Turn yellow to show danger/maximum heat loss\\n  \\n  yield* waitFor(2);\\n\\n  // 3. Growing insulation PAST Critical Radius\\n  yield* insulation().fill(\\\"#2ecc71\\\", 0.5); // Turn green to show it's finally working\\n  yield* heatText().text(\\\"Adding Insulation (Above Critical Radius)\\\\nHeat Loss finally DECREASES\\\", 1);\\n  yield* insulation().size(800, 2, easeInOutCubic);\\n\\n  yield* waitFor(3);\\n});\\n\"","Description":"\"Creating animation scene for Critical Radius\"","Overwrite":"false","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\renu5\\\\Downloads\\\\college\\\\College sem 5\\\\my-animation\\\\src\\\\scenes\\\\radius.tsx\"","toolAction":"\"Writing animation scene\"","toolSummary":"\"Create animation code\""}}]}
