{"step_index":126,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T19:07:32Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-08-31T19:07:32Z sender=4551fb39-02d9-42f5-94e5-3c67c19a3b89 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=I have researched the licensing for Motion Canvas (motioncanvas.io). \n\n**Definitive Answer:**\nYes, Motion Canvas is **100% free for commercial use**. \n\n**Key Licensing Details:**\n1. **MIT License:** The Motion Canvas software itself is fully open-source and released under the MIT License. This grants you the freedom to use, modify, and distribute the software for any purpose.\n2. **No Paid Tiers or Enterprise Editions:** Unlike some competitors (such as Remotion, which requires a paid company license for commercial use at scale), Motion Canvas does not have any paid subscriptions, enterprise tiers, or licensing fees. It is completely free.\n3. **Full Rights to Your Animations:** The MIT license applies to the underlying tool, not to the animations you create. You retain 100% ownership and full rights to all videos and animations generated using Motion Canvas, and you can monetize them or use them in commercial projects without any restrictions or royalties.\n\nSources:\n- [Motion Canvas Official Site](https://motioncanvas.io/)\n- [Motion Canvas GitHub Repository](https://github.com/motion-canvas/motion-canvas) (License: MIT)\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
