{"step_index":134,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T19:39:34Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-01T01:09:34+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-01T01:09:34+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/config/skills/find-skills/SKILL.md`\nTotal Lines: 204\nTotal Bytes: 7106\nShowing lines 1 to 204\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: name: find-skills\n3: description: Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like \"how do I do X\", \"find a skill for X\", \"is there a skill that can...\", or express interest in extending capabilities. This skill should be used when the user is looking for functionality that might exist as an installable skill.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Find Skills (Windows Compatible Version)\n7: \n8: This skill helps you discover and install skills from the open agent skills ecosystem.\n9: \n10: **This is a Windows-compatible fork that fixes the empty output issue in Claude Code on Windows.**\n11: \n12: ## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Windows Compatibility\n13: \n14: **On Windows, you MUST use PowerShell to run skills commands!**\n15: \n16: The default Bash/Git Bash environment on Windows does NOT work with `npx skills` - commands will return empty output.\n17: \n18: **Always use this format on Windows:**\n19: ```bash\n20: powershell -Command \"npx skills find '[query]'\"\n21: powershell -Command \"npx skills add [package] -g -y\"\n22: powershell -Command \"npx skills list -g\"\n23: ```\n24: \n25: **Example:**\n26: ```bash\n27: # ❌ WRONG - will return empty on Windows\n28: npx skills find \"react\"\n29: \n30: # ✅ CORRECT - works on Windows\n31: powershell -Command \"npx skills find 'react'\"\n32: ```\n33: \n34: ## When to Use This Skill\n35: \n36: Use this skill when the user:\n37: \n38: - Asks \"how do I do X\" where X might be a common task with an existing skill\n39: - Says \"find a skill for X\" or \"is there a skill for X\"\n40: - Asks \"can you do X\" where X is a specialized capability\n41: - Expresses inter\n<truncated 4462 bytes>\nds |\n155: | ------------- | ---------------- |\n156: | 数据分析 | data analysis |\n157: | 做PPT | ppt, presentation |\n158: | 写文章 | writing |\n159: | 代码审查 | code review |\n160: | 部署上线 | deploy, deployment |\n161: | 写测试 | testing |\n162: | 做视频 | video, remotion |\n163: \n164: ## Tips for Effective Searches\n165: \n166: 1. **Use specific keywords**: \"react testing\" is better than just \"testing\"\n167: 2. **Try alternative terms**: If \"deploy\" doesn't work, try \"deployment\" or \"ci-cd\"\n168: 3. **Check popular sources**: Many skills come from `vercel-labs/agent-skills` or `ComposioHQ/awesome-claude-skills`\n169: 4. **Use English keywords**: Chinese search will return empty results\n170: \n171: ## When No Skills Are Found\n172: \n173: If no relevant skills exist:\n174: \n175: 1. Acknowledge that no existing skill was found\n176: 2. Offer to help with the task directly using your general capabilities\n177: 3. Suggest the user could create their own skill with `npx skills init`\n178: \n179: Example:\n180: \n181: ```\n182: I searched for skills related to \"xyz\" but didn't find any matches.\n183: I can still help you with this task directly! Would you like me to proceed?\n184: \n185: If this is something you do often, you could create your own skill:\n186: powershell -Command \"npx skills init my-xyz-skill\"\n187: ```\n188: \n189: ## Troubleshooting\n190: \n191: ### Q: Search returns empty on Windows?\n192: A: Make sure you're using `powershell -Command \"npx skills find '...'\"` format, not direct `npx skills find`.\n193: \n194: ### Q: Chinese search returns nothing?\n195: A: Search only supports English keywords. Translate your query to English first.\n196: \n197: ### Q: How to verify installation?\n198: A: Run `powers